  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Kia Optima?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. It reports the Fuel Percentage signal (powertrainFuelSystemRelativeLevel), which you can query through the Telemetry API with a Vehicle JWT. The device also lists a refuel event, which the segments query can detect with the refuel mechanism."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Kia Optima with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device. Once the owner shares the vehicle with your Developer License, exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API. Then query the Telemetry API for that vehicle."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I get check-engine light alerts for a Kia Optima?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device, which lists the dtc event and the Diagnostic Trouble Codes signal (obdDTCList). The Vehicle Triggers API (webhooks) sends a POST to your targetURL when a condition you configure is met, so you don't have to poll."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Kia Optima?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, which lists the idling event. Query segments in the Telemetry API with the idling detection mechanism, which finds contiguous periods where engine RPM stays in the idle range and requires a DIMO device. You can set maxIdleRpm in the segment config; the default is 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Kia Optima mileage?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, which reports the Odometer signal. Call the Attestation API odometer statement endpoint (POST /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId) with a Vehicle JWT. Then retrieve the resulting rawVC through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO supports the Kia Optima through a DIMO device, for model years 2012 and newer, and this coverage has been tested. DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance. Read the data through the Telemetry API using a Vehicle JWT for a vehicle shared with you."
